e72b6f53782" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1045 "Interpreting the Meaning of the Derivative in Context" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186064979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1050 780.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186064399 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8ea4ae18-ffc0-59bc-9ddc-fdba78903ea0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186063091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48935" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1071 "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t)=6\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=4\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2012?$ Round your answer to the nearest integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7cc5ee70-2b10-5325-a2dc-cd7c11e6d8be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064839 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change in the crocodile population $t$ years since $2000$ is equal to the birth rate minus the death rate, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2012$ is $12$ years after $2000$, we have $t=12.$ Substituting $t=12,$ the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river  in $2012$ was\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(12)-D(12) & =6\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)}-4\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)} \\\\  & =6{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3} \\\\  & ≈40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river in $2012$ is approximately $40$ crocodiles per year." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064979 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064979 #edb/ref 1061 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064979 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "31d20aff-dfc8-5c40-ac4f-e90082ea3b22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064979 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064980 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186064981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064980 #edb/ref 1061 1041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064980 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16f4f430-8d96-53e9-8d8a-f9c5dacb8f75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064980 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064981 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186064982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064981 #edb/ref 1061 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064981 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53feca1f-08af-5384-9bcc-951619d23c04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064981 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064982 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064982 #edb/ref 1061 1048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064982 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce4a6a9b-f1e7-5114-a5dd-312034e232c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064982 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065155 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186064980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065155 #edb/ref 1061 22692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065155 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "591c3dff-1506-54a5-a8fe-829db67c140d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065155 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065156 #edb/ref 1061 22693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065156 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "90f0715b-ebb7-53b3-8e60-ab2cec7bd6e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065156 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065394 #edb/ref 1064 "Derivatives naturally occur in many real-world situations, so it's essential to know their units of measurement. The key is to remember that the derivative represents a rate of change.\n\nFor instance, suppose that the temperature of a pizza $t$ minutes after coming out of a hot oven is $T(t)$ degrees Fahrenheit. What are the units of $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}T}{\\textrm{d}t}?$\n\nFirst, we have that the temperature $T(t)$ is measured in degrees Fahrenheit and the time $t$ is measured in minutes.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t): & \\text{degrees Fahrenheit} \\\\ t: & \\text{minutes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\color{black}T}{\\textrm{d}\\color{black}t}$ measures a change in ${\\color{black}T}$ over a change in ${\\color{black}t}.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{degrees Fahrenheit}}{\\text{minutes}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\color{black}T}{\\textrm{d}\\color{black}t}$ is measured in \"degrees Fahrenheit per minute\", or $^\\circ \\textrm F / \\textrm {min}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065394 #edb/ref 1065 552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065394 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1a148fb4-165b-500a-b7e6-a3c9c2776ae8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065394 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327037 #edb/ref 1080 "The distance traveled increased by $10$ meters during the first $30$ seconds" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327037 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0be07498-8050-537a-b25e-fd95bab4699a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327641 #edb/ref 1080 "The distance traveled increased at a constant rate of $3$ meters per second" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327641 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327641 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "51437d5b-5e6c-5066-b244-e7e818095097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327987 #edb/ref 1080 "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled decreased at a rate of $10$ meters per second" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327987 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327987 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7aadd70b-53c1-50fb-bc02-b723b6f3ea3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328410 #edb/ref 1080 "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the car traveled $10$ meters." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328410 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328410 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aaa8d265-16ad-5285-82fb-8aa43f6dd27f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328858 #edb/ref 1080 "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328858 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328858 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc11c238-8417-5632-881c-cdb922cfb484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186328858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329631 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ffcaa0c5-cbb7-57a1-b1e2-92acc3accb1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329907 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329907 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48688" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329907 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329907 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $x(t)$ models the number of meters traveled by a car, $t$ seconds after it sets off on a journey. What is the best interpretation of ${x}^{′}(30)=10?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329907 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce5be28b-4511-5653-9464-457a2f9e4167" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329907 #edb/ref 1074 "The function ${x}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of meters is changing at the moment $t$ seconds after starting its journey.\n\nTherefore, ${x}^{′}(30)=10$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1045 "Interpreting the Meaning of the Derivative in Context" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186515668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514856 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "3bdd210c-9c04-5e69-a3ac-cdfe8109d5df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514908 #edb/ref 1080 "At $10$ degrees Celsius, the resistivity of the wire decreases at a rate of $0.01$ units per degree" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514908 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1071b292-1c48-516f-adc9-50669f444bd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515064 #edb/ref 1080 "At $10$ degrees Celsius, the resistivity of the wire is $0.01$ units less than its value at ${0}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515064 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515064 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "55c40cb2-7242-57e4-a518-1d8459f9122c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515346 #edb/ref 1080 "At $10$ degrees Celsius, the resistivity of the wire is $0.01$ units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515346 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515346 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e35b0b0f-5813-594b-9eea-774b722ff5ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515351 #edb/ref 1080 "At $10$ degrees Celsius, the resistivity of the wire increases at a rate of $0.01$ units per degree" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515351 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515351 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e4b5bf6c-a912-5724-a3ac-e6ee153cd77d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515395 #edb/ref 1080 "For each interval of $10$ degrees Celsius, the resistivity of the wire decreases by $0.01$ units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515395 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515395 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f895225b-6973-503a-8662-72877ccbd1b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186514908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515456 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7b611e52-ac20-5642-b35b-9cb7a57a497c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515612 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515612 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515612 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515612 #edb/ref 1071 "The electrical resistivity of a copper wire varies with the temperature. The function $R(T)$ gives the resistivity of a wire at a temperature of $T$ degrees Celsius. What is the best interpretation of ${R}^{′}(10)=-0.01?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515612 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7907942-0453-56fa-81c8-7f3d98729c3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515612 #edb/ref 1074 "The function ${R}^{′}(T)$ represents the rate at which the resistivity of the wire is decreasing at $T$ degrees Celsius.\n\nTherefore, since it is negative, ${R}^{′}(10)=-0.01$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *At $10$ degrees Celsius, the resistivity of the wire decreases at a rate of $0.01$ units per degree.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515629 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0e00795a-bf92-5c91-9599-9b3a42d17f2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515629 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186515612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515633 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515633 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "15d5622f-a373-5ea6-99ae-45dd9cf87f84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515633 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515668 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515668 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "90ed548d-7b9f-5b06-a9d7-d32c049ddb79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515668 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329907 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
